SwiftPutty local patch 0005
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); suitable for upstreaming

ssh/common.c: clear a BPP's packet queues when freeing it.

ssh_bpp_free() freed the BPP but not the packets still in its in_pq and
out_pq. Packets wait there whenever the protocol layer above has paused,
for example while the user is looking at the host key dialog during key
exchange. Closing the session at that point leaked them. Upstream
frontends end the whole process with the session, so it went unnoticed;
SwiftPutty closes sessions inside a long-running process. Found by
`leaks --atExit`.

pq_in_clear() first detaches the queue from the (already freed) layer
that consumed it, then hands the packets to the global free queue;
pq_out_clear() frees outgoing packets directly. The version-string BPP
freed during protocol setup has empty queues, so that path is unchanged.

--- a/ssh/common.c
+++ b/ssh/common.c
@@ -795,6 +795,8 @@
 void ssh_bpp_free(BinaryPacketProtocol *bpp)
 {
     delete_callbacks_for_context(bpp);
+    pq_in_clear(&bpp->in_pq);
+    pq_out_clear(&bpp->out_pq);
     bpp->vt->free(bpp);
 }
 
